      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Sounds like the avatar has write defaults off and the animations are interruptable. Means other animations can override them mid-playback if their conditions become true. You need to ensure the animation cant be interrupted, easiest way to do this is to just reset the transition settings to default.\nThen you need to set your gesture logic up in a way that lets the affected blendshapes of a playing animation be reset by any animation that could play after it. If you want to do all this automatically without hassle, check out https://hai-vr.github.io/combo-gesture-expressions-av3/",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-10-20T16:51:29.404Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For some unusual reason, whenever I use a hand gesture to change from one facial expression to another, sometimes my blendshapes can get stuck before fully transitioning to the next expression. This leads to anomalies such as half-closed eyes, slightly open mouth, etc. I've tried a multitude of solutions but nothing seems to have helped. The last thing I have to try is a simple \"reset\" state that executes before changing expressions, which I assume would fix the problem. I was only wondering if anyone here had a similar issue and an answer as to why this behavior happens. It's only been affecting one model out of many others I've uploaded. Anyone that could shed light on this issue, I'd be very grateful!",
